Generate_Surface_Normals: reconstruct the two unrecovered switch jumptables

Ghidra could not recover the switches at 0x426943/0x42696f ("Too many branches") and
rendered them as indirect CALLS to raw intra-function labels + return -> execute-fault
0x42694a on L1-7 (the arms are jump targets, not functions).
Reconstruction from dd2h.exe disasm (tables @0x426870/0x426894, 9 dword entries each,
index = local_2c = strip_width-1, guarded by local_2c<9):
- table1 (first strip row) entries [0..8] = {94a,9a7,94a,9a7,959,94a,959,94a,94a}:
  0x42694a re-checks local_1c and picks the DEFAULT vertex selection (= fall-through
  path) -> default case; 0x4269a7 = the local_1c!=0 selection unconditionally
  (iVar2=local_14,iVar5=iVar8,iVar6=iVar7) -> cases 1,3; 0x426959 = eax=local_14,
  edx=local_18, ebx=esi(iVar7) -> cases 4,6.
- table2 (last strip row) entries = {976,976,985,985,976,98f,98f,976,976}: 0x426976 =
  default; 0x426985 = eax=local_14, edx=edi(iVar8), ebx=local_18 -> cases 2,3;
  0x42698f = eax=edi(iVar8), edx=local_18, ebx=esi(iVar7) -> cases 5,6.
  Register->C mapping (from the common code at 0x4269ae): eax=iVar2 (shared vertex),
  edx=iVar5 (edge1 end), ebx=iVar6 (edge2 end); esi=iVar7, edi=iVar8.
The arms then JUMP into the common edge/cross/normalize code (NOT return) -> modeled
as index overrides before the shared computation.
ALSO rewires the cross-product to the contiguous arrays the W:edge1/W:edge2 patches
introduced: asm calls 0x414db8(&edge2,&edge1,&out)=OuterProduct12 with edge1@[ebp-0x6c]
=_e1, edge2@[ebp-0x5c]=_e2, out@[ebp-0x4c]=_n; result stores read _n[0..2]
(previously still read the stale scattered locals local_50/4c/48 = UB), and drops the
leftover scratch copy local_40=local_6c from the pre-array chain.

